## Definition Of Done

- Valid `media-control` stream snapshots use the same normalization and backend-scoped clock as explicit samples and update both hosts immediately.
- App-originated pause is covered by a deterministic regression that does not resolve a fallback refresh to pass.
- Stream termination emits one immediate recovery request, restarts with bounded backoff, and cannot leak callbacks after disposal.
- Provider sampling, transport execution, artwork enrichment, and UI projection no longer share a global exclusion latch.
- Repeated transport input during delayed sampling is represented, ordered or safely coalesced by documented rules, and every returned promise settles.
- Each backend owns isolated clock state; no module-global playback clock remains.
- Artwork completion independently updates only the matching presentation and preserves existing Kitty rendering behavior.
- Streaming providers retain one bounded recovery poll; `nowplaying-cli` remains polling-only with 3/5/8-second state-based bounds.
- OpenCode and Pi lifecycle tests prove subscription, timer, in-flight result, artwork, and queued-intent cleanup.
- Existing OpenCode controller entry points, Pi commands/shortcuts, `MusicBackend` consumers, package exports, and smoke installations pass where their contracts remain justified.
- All phase verification commands and the root `bun run check` pass on the new stack based on `fix/music-player-sync`, with PR #40 unchanged.
